<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abaco Islands</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as the Abacos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Abaco Islands are a chain of islands in the northern Bahamas, made up of Great Abaco, Little Abaco and many smaller cays. They were settled largely by Loyalists from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> after the American War of Independence, and Marsh Harbour is their main town. In September 2019 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-dorian">Hurricane Dorian</a> struck the Abacos and neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-bahama">Grand Bahama</a>, killing dozens of people and destroying much of their housing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abaco-islands.jpg" alt="Abaco Islands" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: T L Miles · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Districts_of_Abaco_Bahamas.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
